IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ccc-core`
IMPORT `ccc29-xxviii-4-appeal-812`
IMPORT `ccc29-xxviii-5-appeal-829`

-- ccc29-tests-xxviii-5-appeal-829.l4 -- tests for sections 829 to 840 of the Criminal Code (Canada).
-- Every expected value is written from the text before the run, beside its assertion. Argument order is the GIVEN order of each function.

§ `Tests -- sections 829 and 830`

-- 829: in any province, the superior court of criminal jurisdiction; Nunavut judge's appeal: a judge of the Court of Appeal of Nunavut; a territory that is not a province: not covered.
#ASSERT `s 829 the appeal court for sections 830 to 838` `s 812(1) Ontario` FALSE EQUALS JUST `s 829(1) the superior court of criminal jurisdiction for the province`
#ASSERT `s 829 the appeal court for sections 830 to 838` `s 812(1) Alberta` FALSE EQUALS JUST `s 829(1) the superior court of criminal jurisdiction for the province`
#ASSERT `s 829 the appeal court for sections 830 to 838` `s 812(1) Newfoundland and Labrador` FALSE EQUALS JUST `s 829(1) the superior court of criminal jurisdiction for the province`
#ASSERT `s 829 the appeal court for sections 830 to 838` `s 812(1) Nunavut` TRUE EQUALS JUST `s 829(2) a judge of the Court of Appeal of Nunavut`
#ASSERT `s 829 the appeal court for sections 830 to 838` `s 812(1) Ontario` TRUE EQUALS JUST `s 829(2) a judge of the Court of Appeal of Nunavut`
#ASSERT `s 829 the appeal court for sections 830 to 838` `s 812(1) Nunavut` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 829 the appeal court for sections 830 to 838` `s 812(1) Yukon` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 829 the appeal court for sections 830 to 838` `s 812(1) the Northwest Territories` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- 830(1): (the person, the decision, the ground).
#ASSERT `s 830(1) the person may appeal against the decision on the ground` TRUE TRUE `s 830(1)(a) it is erroneous in point of law` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 830(1) the person may appeal against the decision on the ground` TRUE TRUE `s 830(1)(b) it is in excess of jurisdiction` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 830(1) the person may appeal against the decision on the ground` TRUE TRUE `s 830(1)(c) it constitutes a refusal or failure to exercise jurisdiction` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 830(1) the person may appeal against the decision on the ground` TRUE TRUE `s 830(1) another ground` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 830(1) the person may appeal against the decision on the ground` FALSE TRUE `s 830(1)(a) it is erroneous in point of law` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 830(1) the person may appeal against the decision on the ground` TRUE FALSE `s 830(1)(a) it is erroneous in point of law` EQUALS NOTHING
-- 830(2): a transcript unless an agreed statement of facts is filed within fifteen days: (files a statement, days, agreed in writing).
#ASSERT `s 830(2) the appeal is required to be based on a transcript of the proceedings appealed from` FALSE 0 FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 830(2) the appeal is required to be based on a transcript of the proceedings appealed from` TRUE 15 TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 830(2) the appeal is required to be based on a transcript of the proceedings appealed from` TRUE 16 TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 830(2) the appeal is required to be based on a transcript of the proceedings appealed from` TRUE 10 FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- 830(3): (rules of court otherwise providing, days after the date of the decision).
#ASSERT `s 830(3) the notice of appeal is served and filed within thirty days after the date of the decision` FALSE 30 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 830(3) the notice of appeal is served and filed within thirty days after the date of the decision` FALSE 31 EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 830(3) the notice of appeal is served and filed within thirty days after the date of the decision` TRUE 45 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 830(3) the last day for serving and filing the notice of appeal` (Date 1 1 2025) EQUALS Date 31 1 2025
#ASSERT `s 830(4) the Attorney General of Canada has the same rights of appeal as the Attorney General of a province` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 830(4) the Attorney General of Canada has the same rights of appeal as the Attorney General of a province` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Tests -- sections 831 to 838`

-- 831: (the appeal is under 830, the section number).
#ASSERT `s 831 the provision applies to the appeal` TRUE 816 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 831 the provision applies to the appeal` TRUE 817 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 831 the provision applies to the appeal` TRUE 819 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 831 the provision applies to the appeal` TRUE 825 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 831 the provision applies to the appeal` TRUE 818 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 831 the provision applies to the appeal` FALSE 816 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 831 the appeal court is required to give such directions as it thinks necessary for expediting the hearing of the appeal` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 831 the appeal court is required to give such directions as it thinks necessary for expediting the hearing of the appeal` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 831 the appeal court is required to give such directions as it thinks necessary for expediting the hearing of the appeal` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- 832(1): (notice filed under 830, the defendant is the appellant, the course).
#ASSERT `s 832(1) the appeal court may take the course` TRUE TRUE `s 832(1) make a release order as provided in section 816` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 832(1) the appeal court may take the course` TRUE FALSE `s 832(1) make a release order as provided in section 816` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 832(1) the appeal court may take the course` TRUE FALSE `s 832(1) order that the appellant appear before a justice and enter into a recognizance as provided in section 817` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 832(1) the appeal court may take the course` TRUE TRUE `s 832(1) order that the appellant appear before a justice and enter into a recognizance as provided in section 817` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 832(1) the appeal court may take the course` FALSE TRUE `s 832(1) make a release order as provided in section 816` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 832(2) subsection (1) does not apply` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 832(2) subsection (1) does not apply` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 833 a writ of certiorari or other writ is required to remove the conviction, judgment, verdict or other final order or determination` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 833 a writ of certiorari or other writ is required to remove the conviction, judgment, verdict or other final order or determination` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- 834(1): (notice filed, the course, the court considers the order proper).
#ASSERT `s 834(1) the appeal court is required to hear and determine the grounds of appeal` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 834(1) the appeal court is required to hear and determine the grounds of appeal` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 834(1) the appeal court may take the course` TRUE `s 834(1)(a) affirm, reverse or modify the conviction, judgment, verdict or other final order or determination` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 834(1) the appeal court may take the course` TRUE `s 834(1)(b) remit the matter to the summary conviction court with the opinion of the appeal court` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 834(1) the appeal court may take the course` TRUE `s 834(1) make any other order in relation to the matter or with respect to costs` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 834(1) the appeal court may take the course` TRUE `s 834(1) make any other order in relation to the matter or with respect to costs` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 834(1) the appeal court may take the course` FALSE `s 834(1)(a) affirm, reverse or modify the conviction, judgment, verdict or other final order or determination` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 834(2) the authority and jurisdiction may be exercised by a judge of the court sitting in chambers` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 834(2) the authority and jurisdiction may be exercised by a judge of the court sitting in chambers` TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 834(2) the authority and jurisdiction may be exercised by a judge of the court sitting in chambers` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- 835: (decision rendered, the enforcer, affirmed / modified / made).
#ASSERT `s 835(1) the summary conviction court or a justice has the same authority to enforce the conviction, order or determination as if no appeal had been taken` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 835(1) the summary conviction court or a justice has the same authority to enforce the conviction, order or determination as if no appeal had been taken` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 835(1) the summary conviction court or a justice has the same authority to enforce the conviction, order or determination as if no appeal had been taken` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 835(1) the summary conviction court or a justice has the same authority to enforce the conviction, order or determination as if no appeal had been taken` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 835(2) the order may be enforced by the process of the appeal court` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 835(2) the order may be enforced by the process of the appeal court` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 836 the person is taken to have abandoned all rights of appeal under section 813` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 836 the person is taken to have abandoned all rights of appeal under section 813` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 836 the person is taken to have abandoned all rights of appeal under section 813` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 837 no appeal under section 830 lies from the conviction or order` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 837 no appeal under section 830 lies from the conviction or order` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 838 the appeal court or a judge thereof may extend the time period` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 838 the appeal court or a judge thereof may extend the time period` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 838 the appeal court or a judge thereof may extend the time period` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Tests -- sections 839 and 840`

-- 839(1): (the decision, the ground is a question of law alone, leave, the appeal court is the court of appeal).
#ASSERT `s 839(1) an appeal to the court of appeal may be taken against the decision` `s 839(1)(a) a decision of a court in respect of an appeal under section 822` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 839(1) an appeal to the court of appeal may be taken against the decision` `s 839(1)(a) a decision of a court in respect of an appeal under section 822` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
